Package: pulsaros-airpods
Version: 0.2.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Victor Rosario <hello@victorrosario.dev>
Depends: gnome-shell, bluez, libqt6bluetooth6, libqt6core6t64, libqt6dbus6, libqt6gui6, libqt6network6, libqt6qml6, libqt6quick6, libqt6quickcontrols2-6, libqt6widgets6, libpulse0, libssl3t64, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-window
Recommends: pipewire-pulse
Description: AirPods in the GNOME top bar for Pulsar OS.
 Shows an AirPods icon while they are connected, like macOS, with the battery
 of each earbud and the case, the listening mode (Noise Cancellation,
 Transparency, Adaptive, Off where the model has it), Conversation Awareness,
 One-Bud ANC and ear detection.
 .
 Two parts in one package: a GNOME Shell extension (airpods@pulsaros.org, Shell
 48 and 51) and a headless daemon (librepods) that talks to the AirPods over
 Bluetooth and publishes their state. The daemon is a modified copy of the
 omarchy-pods daemon, itself a fork of librepods by Kavish Devar, licensed
 GPL-3.0; see /usr/share/doc/pulsaros-airpods/librepods.
